@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy</PageTitle>

<div class="hiw">
<h1>Privacy</h1>

<p class="hiw-intro">
    Paysys is a demonstration system. Nothing here is real money, and you should not enter real personal or card
    details. This page says what the system holds anyway, why, and what you can do about it.
</p>

<h2 id="privacy-held">What Paysys holds about you</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Your username, and your password as a one-way hash (the password itself is never stored).</li>
    <li>Your payment PIN as a one-way hash, if you set one.</li>
    <li>An email address and a phone number, only if you add them on your profile. They are not verified and are not used to sign you in, to recover an account or to contact you.</li>
    <li>Your accounts, with their balances, the cards linked to them (an opaque token, the last four digits, the brand and the expiry date), your payments and your holds.</li>
    <li>An audit log of actions in the system. Each entry carries an internal user id, not your name.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="privacy-not-held">What Paysys does not hold</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Full card numbers and card security codes. They are checked and swapped for a token, and the number itself is never stored or logged.</li>
    <li>Your real identity. Paysys does not check who you are.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="privacy-why">Why, and who sees it</h2>
<p>
    The data exists only to run the demonstration: to sign you in, move demo money and show you your history.
    It is not sold, shared for advertising or used to profile you. The system runs on Render (the servers),
    Neon (the database, in Frankfurt) and GitHub Pages (this web page).
</p>

<h2 id="privacy-rights">What you can do</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>See and download your data.</strong> Profile, then Your data, then Download my data.</li>
    <li><strong>Correct your contact details.</strong> Profile, then Contact details.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete your account.</strong> Profile, then Your data, then Delete my account. Your name, contact details, PIN and sign-in are removed and your cards are closed. Your accounts must be empty first.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="privacy-kept">What stays after you delete</h2>
<p>
    Records of payments and the audit log stay, because financial records must be kept and the audit log is built so that
    nothing in it can be changed. After deletion they point to an anonymous account and carry no name or contact detail.
</p>

<h2 id="privacy-keep">How long data is kept</h2>
<p>
    Your personal details are kept while your account exists and are removed when you delete it. Payment records and the
    audit log are kept after that. No automatic expiry of unused accounts exists yet.
</p>

<p class="send-hint">Questions about your data: contact the operator of this demonstration, Ismail Aslan.</p>
</div>
